# One command, for the desktop shortcut that collects crash evidence.
#
# Same shape and same reasoning as 50-chiron-ssh one name below: the shortcut
# is tapped on a touchscreen, the tapper is already in the sudo group, and a
# password prompt would mean an on-screen keyboard over a modal dialog for a
# command that same person could run from a shell. What this removes is the
# prompt, not the authority.
#
# The grant is one absolute path with one fixed argument. --manual is the
# collector's manual snapshot mode, which writes one archive onto the tapping
# account's Desktop and reads the journals and the pstore archive; it performs
# no other action. Any other invocation, and every other command, still asks.
%sudo ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/chiron-evidence --manual
